{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Interpretation 1</b><br>Galilee. Of rings [of gold]." "Tarshish. A precious stone, the color of the dawn." "His body — ivory work. Elephants, like worked iron." "<b>Interpretation 2</b><br>His fingers are rings of gold, and the hair upon them he likened to Tarshish." "His abdomen is girded in white garments over-dyed with sapphire, which is red — and the appearance: his Nazirites are bright from snow, white from milk [red of bone from pearls, sapphire is their guise] — and there he places sapphires like pearls, for his words are doubled, and לבנת הספיר is from לבנה (the moon) and not from whiteness, and the word כמעשה is a noun, and it is not fitting to describe his abdomen, for he is not naked." "<b>Interpretation 3</b><br>His hands are rings of gold. They are the spheres; they are the heavens." "In Tarshish. The stars." "His abdomen. The epicycles of the uppermost sphere, and it is the middle (broad) line." "Sapphires. They are the zodiac signs."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:38.087198332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}